usage: execution_request.py [-h] {build} ...

Bind frozen scope, purpose and native request template into a real request.
Contract A. The binding record is an audit-side request index, not an
authorization file: it states the request boundary (profile, byte/time/token/
cost caps, config fingerprints) and never selects a provider or model. Native
request bytes stay exactly the supplied business fields; effective caps are
the smaller of scope and deploy, and any attempted profile or cap
amplification is refused with a specific diagnostic instead of being guessed
or silently clamped.

positional arguments:
  {build}

options:
  -h, --help  show this help message and exit
